 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "My Hotpoint washer dryer isn't drying properly any more and there's a funny smell when it's on the dry bit. Is there something I should clean?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, please start by cleaning the lint filter (usually inside the door rim or at the bottom front) and the condenser (a plastic grille usually behind the filter cover). A 'funny smell' is often scorching fluff from restricted airflow. Once cleaned, try a small load of dry clothes only to see if it dries well."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, I didn't know it needed cleaning. It smells like burning dust, and the top of the machine feels very hot when it's drying. I've kept using it though. Should I be doing that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nA burning smell or smoke can mean an electrical fault or a fire risk. Stop using it, switch it off and unplug it (or turn it off at the fuse box), and don't run it again — not even as a test — until it has been checked by a qualified engineer. Before you start, switch it off and unplug it. Please stop using the machine immediately until it has cooled down completely. The 'burning dust' smell and excessive heat are classic signs that lint is building up on the heating element because airflow is blocked. This is a fire risk. 1. Clean the lint filter (usually inside the door rim or at the bottom front).\n2. Clean the condenser (a plastic grille usually behind the filter cover). Did you find a significant amount of fluff or debris in these areas after cleaning them?"
  }
 ],
